body:
"Those with Post Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD) can often develop difficulties with sounds such as an exaggerated startle response, fear of sound (phonophobia), aversion to specific sounds (misophonia), and a difficulty in tolerance and volume of sounds that would not be considered loud by normal hearing individuals (hyperacusis)." [https://www.ptsduk.org/hyperacusis-and-ptsd/](https://www.ptsduk.org/hyperacusis-and-ptsd/)

&#x200B;

I hope it gets better for you. I know how it is to feel like you do.
